Applied StandardScaler where required
Saved scaler for deployment
5. Machine Learning Models

The following classification algorithms were implemented.

5.1 Logistic Regression

Logistic Regression is a linear classification algorithm that estimates the probability of class membership using the logistic (sigmoid) function.

Advantages
Fast
Simple
Interpretable
5.2 Decision Tree

Decision Trees classify data using a tree-like structure consisting of decision nodes and leaf nodes.

Advantages
Easy to visualize
Handles nonlinear data
Requires little preprocessing
5.3 K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)

KNN classifies a sample based on the majority class among its nearest neighbors.

Advantages
Easy to implement
Effective for small and medium-sized datasets
5.4 Gaussian Naive Bayes

Naive Bayes applies Bayes' Theorem while assuming independence among features.

Advantages
Fast
Computationally efficient
Performs well for probabilistic classification
5.5 Random Forest

Random Forest is an ensemble learning algorithm that combines multiple Decision Trees to improve prediction accuracy.

Advantages
High accuracy
Reduces overfitting
Handles complex datasets effectively
6. Evaluation Metrics

The following evaluation metrics were used to compare model performance.

Accuracy

Measures the proportion of correctly classified instances.

Precision

Measures the proportion of correctly predicted positive cases.

Recall

Measures the proportion of actual positive cases correctly identified.

F1 Score

Harmonic mean of Precision and Recall.

ROC-AUC Score

Measures the ability of the classifier to distinguish between positive and negative classes.

Matthews Correlation Coefficient (MCC)

Provides a balanced evaluation metric even when classes are imbalanced.

