8. Model Observations
Logistic Regression

Provided a strong baseline model with good interpretability and competitive performance.

Decision Tree

Captured nonlinear relationships but may overfit if the tree becomes too deep.

K-Nearest Neighbors

Produced reliable predictions after feature scaling but required more computation during prediction.

Gaussian Naive Bayes

Very fast and computationally efficient but assumes feature independence.

Random Forest

Generally achieved the best balance between accuracy and robustness due to ensemble learning.

